WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.860
Bengal, eighteen sixty.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:04.920
A play holds up a mirror.

3
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.040
Its name:

4
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.990
Nil Darpan, the Indigo Mirror.

5
00:00:09.527 --> 00:00:11.727
In March eighteen fifty nine,

6
00:00:11.727 --> 00:00:13.707
thousands of ryots had refused

7
00:00:13.707 --> 00:00:16.347
to grow indigo, a crop forced on

8
00:00:16.347 --> 00:00:17.817
them through advances.

9
00:00:18.495 --> 00:00:20.515
One farmer told the Indigo

10
00:00:20.515 --> 00:00:22.875
Commission: I would rather beg

11
00:00:22.875 --> 00:00:24.525
than sow indigo.

12
00:00:24.937 --> 00:00:26.937
Dinabandhu Mitra turned this

13
00:00:26.937 --> 00:00:28.137
into a drama.

14
00:00:28.137 --> 00:00:30.537
A peasant family, happy on its

15
00:00:30.537 --> 00:00:32.717
land, ruined by indigo.

16
00:00:32.717 --> 00:00:34.837
It came out in Dhaka, without

17
00:00:34.837 --> 00:00:35.987
his name.

18
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.090
His preface spoke to the

19
00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:39.690
planters directly.

20
00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.310
Here is a mirror.

21
00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:42.910
Look at your face.

22
00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:44.650
They did not enjoy the

23
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:45.660
reflection.

24
00:00:46.311 --> 00:00:48.511
In eighteen sixty one came an

25
00:00:48.511 --> 00:00:50.151
English translation.

26
00:00:50.151 --> 00:00:52.431
The missionary James Long had it

27
00:00:52.431 --> 00:00:54.531
printed, with his own note in

28
00:00:54.531 --> 00:00:55.331
front.

29
00:00:55.711 --> 00:00:57.491
The planters went to court.

30
00:00:57.491 --> 00:01:00.371
In July, at Calcutta's Supreme

31
00:01:00.371 --> 00:01:02.971
Court, Long was found guilty of

32
00:01:02.971 --> 00:01:05.471
libel. A fine of one thousand

33
00:01:05.471 --> 00:01:07.981
rupees, and a month in jail.

34
00:01:08.512 --> 00:01:10.612
Then Kaliprasanna Sinha paid the

35
00:01:10.612 --> 00:01:12.632
fine, right there in court.

36
00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.222
Long still served his month.

37
00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:17.057
For GS1:

38
00:01:17.057 --> 00:01:19.090
the Indigo revolt of eighteen

39
00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:19.817
fifty nine;

40
00:01:19.817 --> 00:01:22.770
the Indigo Commission, which let

41
00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.130
ryots refuse indigo;

42
00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:26.850
and Nil Darpan, which carried

43
00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.680
the fields into the city.

44
00:01:29.446 --> 00:01:30.606
A field.

45
00:01:30.606 --> 00:01:31.646
A play.

46
00:01:31.646 --> 00:01:33.006
A courtroom.

47
00:01:33.006 --> 00:01:35.066
And a mirror nobody could put

48
00:01:35.066 --> 00:01:35.936
down.
